Reject value-mapped codebooks with zero dimensions.

Our own patch (AvP): the part of CVE-2008-1419 that libvorbis 1.3.7, and
upstream main at 1b75110b5a, still have. See the comment in the code.

--- a/lib/codebook.c
+++ b/lib/codebook.c
@@ -229,6 +229,19 @@
     /* implicitly populated value mapping */
     /* explicitly populated value mapping */
 
+    /* A book with a value mapping turns each code into a list of 'dim'
+       numbers. A list of zero numbers makes no sense, and libvorbis's own
+       encoder never writes one (all its built-in books have dim of 1 or
+       more). Only a damaged or deliberately crafted file has one, and the
+       decoder cannot cope with it: building a type 1 book would never finish
+       (_book_maptype1_quantvals loops forever), and reading audio through
+       such a book in a type 0 residue would divide by zero and crash
+       (vorbis_book_decodevs_add). So the file is refused here, while its
+       setup is being read, before either can happen. This is what is left of
+       CVE-2008-1419: the older checks only cover floor 0 books and residue
+       phrasebooks. */
+    if(s->dim==0)goto _eofout;
+
     s->q_min=oggpack_read(opb,32);
     s->q_delta=oggpack_read(opb,32);
     s->q_quant=oggpack_read(opb,4)+1;
